  'Advance tax plan': { what: 'How this year\'s taxable income and credits are worked out.', how: 'The profit so far is scaled up by days to a full year, or replaced by your estimate. Adjustments add back costs tax does not allow (positive) or take off deductions (negative). Payments are the posted debits to the advance tax account; credits are the debits to the TDS account, plus other credits you enter.' },
  'Tax for the year': { what: 'The tax on the year\'s taxable income at the chosen rate, with surcharge, marginal relief and 4% cess, less tax credits.', how: 'Income and tax are rounded to the nearest ten rupees. Rates change with each Finance Act: check them against the year\'s Act. No advance tax is due when the tax after credits is under ₹10,000.' },
  'Advance tax instalments': { what: 'The four dates (15 June, 15 September, 15 December, 15 March) with the share of the year\'s tax due by each and what was paid by then.', how: 'Pay the amount to pay by the date, then post the payment to the advance tax account (and mark the item paid in the Compliance calendar with the challan). Short means less was paid by a date that has passed; interest on it is not worked out here.' },
